  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "letting go of anger through compassion" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cognitive-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A short reflective exercise for someone who has wronged you: you keep the wrong in view but deliberately see the offender as a whole, flawed human being who needs to change, and try to wish them well, instead of replaying the hurt." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/compassion-and-relationships> .
