<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I rehearsing a possible loss in order to prepare and appreciate, or am I just worrying?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "After imagining this loss, did I come back to what I still have and what I can do now?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Which parts of the outcome I fear are actually up to me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Once, I'll list what could go wrong in the presentation, prepare for the questions I can foresee, and accept that the reaction isn't fully up to me. And I'll take a minute to picture not having this job at all, then notice what I'd miss." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I'll keep replaying how badly the presentation could go every night until then, and keep grumbling about this job." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "Your manager asks you to present to senior leadership next week, and you also have a job you mostly enjoy but have started to complain about." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "A brief, bounded rehearsal turns vague fear into preparation and restores appreciation, whereas dwelling on the worst only adds suffering before anything has happened." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose one thing you value and tend to take for granted, such as a relationship, your health, your job or an ordinary comfort." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Remind yourself plainly of its nature, starting small, for example that this mug can break and that the people you love are mortal." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "For a minute or two, imagine concretely what your life would be like without it, or how it might never have come about." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Return to the present and notice that you do still have it; name one way you will use or appreciate it today." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Before a risky plan, list what could go wrong, separate what is up to you from what is not, and prepare for the parts you can influence." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Stop if the exercise turns into dread or repetitive worry, and shorten it or set it aside." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Negative visualization" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Practice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Negative visualization" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "praemeditatio malorum" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "premeditatio malorum" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "premeditation of evils" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "premeditation of future evils" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "rehearsal of misfortune" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/spiritual-exercises> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/negative-visualization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Stoic exercise of deliberately imagining that you could lose what you value, or that a setback could happen, so that you hold good things with more appreciation and meet misfortune with less shock." .
